     *  (a negative amount), the one of the number given, which must be a settled claim of the person,
     *  or else it is refused; refused as well when it exceeds what remains of that claim: its amount
     *  less the corrections already made against it (VOID and DELETED ones, and the claim being
     *  edited, left out). */
    private Claim corrected(String sheetId, long personId, BigDecimal amount, String corrects, Long editing) {
        if (amount.signum() >= 0) {
            return null;
        }
        Claim corrected = (corrects == null ? Optional.<Claim>empty()
                : claims.findBySheetIdAndPersonIdAndNumberAndStatus(sheetId, personId, corrects, ClaimStatus.SETTLED))
                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
